<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schoemansdal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1848–1867</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Zoutpansbergdorp</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Schoemansdal was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> settlement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soutpansberg">Soutpansberg</a> in the far north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a>, founded in 1848 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-hendrik-potgieter">Andries Hendrik Potgieter</a>'s followers and later named after the commandant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephanus-schoeman">Stephanus Schoeman</a>. It became a frontier centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> trade and the seat of the Zoutpansberg republic. Under pressure from Venda resistance led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makhado">Makhado</a>, it was abandoned and burned in 1867. Its site is now an open-air museum.</p></div>
